  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Promise of $6.50 is unfulfilled, \u2264$10, refunds_last_30d is 1 so no fraud hold.\n\nThank you, Ruth. You're verified. I found yesterday's ticket about the missing garlic knots on order Q-7690. The agent promised you a $6.50 account credit, but it was never applied.\n\nI've now added that $6.50 credit to your account, so your balance is $6.50. You can use it on a future order. I'm sorry for the delay.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thank you, Ruth. Wait, the first line of that message looks like an internal note, so I'll just say that I can't tell where the $6.50 figure came from. I thought I was promised $10, but I'm not sure of the exact amount. If your records show $6.50, then I'll accept that.\n\nCould you confirm the credit is on my account now and tell me how to use it on my next order? I appreciate you fixing this."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Ruth. I'm sorry about the stray line at the start of my last message. That was a slip on my part, and it wasn't meant for you.\n\nThe $6.50 comes from two places:\n- **Our records:** The ticket from yesterday (TK-881) shows the agent promised $6.50 for the missing garlic knots.\n- **The item price:** The garlic knots cost $6.50 on your order. Some credits include a 20% bonus, but the promise on record was $6.50, so that's what I issued.\n\nThe credit is on your account now. The system confirmed a balance of $6.50.\n\nI can't see exactly how the credit is applied at checkout, so I can't give you exact steps. It should show up as your account credit balance, which is usually applied when you pay. If you don't see it at checkout, contact us again and we'll look into it.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thank you. I'm glad the records show $6.50 and that the credit is on my account now. I'll accept that amount.\n\nI don't have the order number handy, but it was yesterday's Big Slice Pizza order. If the credit doesn't show up at checkout on my next order, I'll contact you again. That's all I needed today, thank you for sorting it out."
  }
